From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:24:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-media: decoder mode: offer scaled frames, keep more of
 them

The decoder mode offers its SAND frames to the display (q11-071) only
when the frame is the guest buffer's size: a stream wider than
host-max-width (q11-076), 4K into DomA's 1080p buffers, was converted
by the GPU on every frame, scaling as it went.

With /run/qemu-sand-scaled such a frame is offered too, at its own
size, with the guest buffer's size as the texture area it fills
(DirectScanout.src_w/src_h), and the display hands it to weston, whose
HVS plane scales it (q11-081, or SDL's viewport when it is shown alone
full screen). That is what the Raspberry Pi 4's proxy does with the
codec's buffers.

The references kept for the display are bounded by 384 MiB instead of
128. A WebView playing a 4K60 stream shows a frame some 21-24 frames
after its decode; a frame shown after its reference went is converted
late, which delays the next ones further. With 256 MiB (21 frames of
12.4 MB) the frames shown a second swung between 25.6 and 42.4 from run
to run, with 900-1400 late conversions in the bad runs; with 384 MiB the
pool's own bound (24 frames here) decides, and eight runs gave
41.8-43.9, full screen and among the HMI, with 16-28 late. The pool
shares DomD's CMA, which the rpi5 layer raises to 640 MiB with this;
CmaFree's lowest was 23-49 MB in those runs, and 56 kB in an earlier
run of a test build with the same bound. The Raspberry Pi 5's Linux
Dom0 flavour gives DomA no virtio-media decoder (XT_DOMA_HWDEC_VULKAN
is false there), so this does not apply to it.

When the decoder lets the display's entries go (input stopped, a new
pool, another size, a full import cache, the GPU path failing, close),
the conversions it skipped are made first, from the references still
held, instead of leaving those guest buffers stale; that waits for the
GPU on the main loop, at most once per 12 conversions. The stop's
statistics line no longer counts conversions still skipped, which is
now always 0.

Measured on a 16 GB Raspberry Pi 5 running the 8g image (2026-10-19),
codec -T of a 4K60 HEVC stream alone full screen: 49.3 fps, V3D render
92% before (CMA 384 MiB, DomA's scanout buffers not linear) against
59.6 fps, 41% with this, CMA 640 MiB and linear buffers,
weston's GPU time 38% -> under 2%, the whole picture on the panel
(checked with a camera). The WebView figures are in q11-081.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 hw/virtio/virtio-media-decoder.c | 61 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/virtio/virtio-media-decoder.c b/hw/virtio/virtio-media-decoder.c
index 673b7cd..986311b 100644
--- a/hw/virtio/virtio-media-decoder.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/virtio-media-decoder.c
@@ -198,16 +198,23 @@ typedef struct DecGpuEntry {
  * bounded as a share of the CMA the pool lives in: at most this many bytes'
  * worth, between 2 and DEC_DS_REFS_MAX frames; beyond that one goes
  * (dec_ds_keep says which), and that frame is shown from the guest's copy
- * instead.
+ * instead. 384 MiB lets the pool's bound decide (ds_refs_cap; for frames of
+ * 12 MB or less it is the tighter one -- a 4K frame is 12.4 MB, and the
+ * Raspberry Pi 5 kept 24 of them): a WebView playing a 4K60 stream
+ * shows a frame some 21-24 frames after its decode, and with 256 MiB (21 frames)
+ * it showed 25.6-42.4 frames a second, swinging between runs -- each frame
+ * shown after its reference went needs the late conversion, which delays the
+ * next ones further -- against 41.8-43.9 in eight runs with 384, full screen
+ * and among the HMI (CMA 640 MiB, CmaFree's lowest 23-49 MB, 2026-10-19).
  */
-#define DEC_DS_REFS_BYTES (128u << 20)
+#define DEC_DS_REFS_BYTES (384u << 20)
 #define DEC_DS_REFS_MAX 32
 /*
  * The references cost the pool's CMA, so they are kept only while the display
  * takes the buffers: after a start, or once it stopped taking them, for
- * DEC_DS_PROBE_MS, and then again every DEC_DS_RETRY_MS (a video that is not
- * full screen, or not the window's size -- a 4K one in a 1080p window -- is
- * never taken).
+ * DEC_DS_PROBE_MS, and then again every DEC_DS_RETRY_MS (a video that is
+ * neither full screen nor, with /run/qemu-plane-sand, on a plane the display
+ * hands to the compositor is never taken).
  *
  * The limits of that probe: the pool keeps every buffer it allocated until the
  * stream stops (v4l2request never frees one), so a probe that grew it leaves
@@ -826,8 +833,9 @@ static void dec_gpu_hold(VirtIOMediaDec *d, const AVFrame *fr, void *handle)
  * guest buffer it was converted into, so that weston puts a full-screen frame
  * on an HVS plane; this is the same for the decoder's (v4l2request) buffers.
  * The display (ui/sdl2-gl.c, sdl2-wl-scanout.c) takes the buffer instead of the
- * guest's copy only when the guest scans that copy out full screen and alone
- * (/run/qemu-isp-scanout); otherwise the copy is shown as before.
+ * guest's copy when the guest scans that copy out full screen and alone
+ * (/run/qemu-isp-scanout), or on one of the planes it hands to the compositor
+ * (/run/qemu-plane-sand); otherwise the copy is shown as before.
  *
  * Unlike the proxy's, the pixels live in libavcodec's pool, not in a buffer the
  * guest queues: a frame stays showable while a reference to it is kept, and the
@@ -864,6 +872,20 @@ static bool dec_ds_skip_on(void)
     return dec_ds_file_on("/run/qemu-sand-skip-isp", &checked, &on);
 }
 
+/*
+ * q11-dec-sand-scaled: /run/qemu-sand-scaled offers a frame host-max-width
+ * scaled for the guest too (a 4K stream into a 1080p buffer). The display gets
+ * the decoder's buffer at the frame's size and the compositor scales it, on the
+ * HVS, as the RPi4's proxy does with the codec's buffers.
+ */
+static bool dec_ds_scaled_on(void)
+{
+    static int64_t checked = -1000000;
+    static bool on;
+
+    return dec_ds_file_on("/run/qemu-sand-scaled", &checked, &on);
+}
+
 static uint64_t dec_ds_epochs;
 
 static bool dec_ds_current(void *owner, uint32_t slot, uint64_t seq)
@@ -1146,13 +1168,21 @@ static void dec_ds_drop(VirtIOMediaDec *d)
         direct_scanout_forget(d);
         d->ds_epoch = 0;
     }
+    /*
+     * q11-dec-sand-scanout: the guest buffers whose conversion was skipped get it
+     * now, while the references are still here, or they keep stale content once
+     * the display stops taking this owner's buffers. Each pass of up to
+     * DEC_DS_CATCH_MAX waits for its GPU work, here on the main loop.
+     */
+    while (d->ds_pend_n) {
+        dec_ds_catch_up(d);
+    }
     if (d->ds_pub_n) {
         info_report("virtio-media/dec: sand-scanout: %" PRIu64 " offered, %"
                     PRIu64 " conversions skipped, %" PRIu64 " made late, %"
-                    PRIu64 " lost, %u still skipped at the stop, %" PRIu64
-                    " let go before their release, %" PRIu64 " evicted on "
-                    "screen, %" PRIu64 " pool waits given up", d->ds_pub_n,
-                    d->ds_skip_n, d->ds_catch_n, d->ds_lost_n, d->ds_pend_n,
+                    PRIu64 " lost, %" PRIu64 " let go before their release, %"
+                    PRIu64 " evicted on screen, %" PRIu64 " pool waits given up",
+                    d->ds_pub_n, d->ds_skip_n, d->ds_catch_n, d->ds_lost_n,
                     d->ds_evict_release_n, d->ds_evict_held_n, d->ds_starved_n);
         d->ds_pub_n = d->ds_skip_n = d->ds_catch_n = d->ds_lost_n = 0;
         d->ds_evict_held_n = d->ds_starved_n = d->ds_evict_release_n = 0;
@@ -1411,9 +1441,9 @@ static int dec_gpu_write(VirtIOMediaSession *s, VirtIOMediaBuffer *gb,
     /* q11-dec-sand-scanout: offer the decoder's buffer to the display */
     assert(!d->thr_on);   /* avctx below: a hwaccel codec has no decode thread */
     tex = virtio_media_gpu_res_tex(gb->virgl_res);
-    /* q11-dec-scale: the display shows a buffer 1:1, so not a scaled one */
-    show = !scaled && tex && dec_ds_on() && direct_scanout_sand_usable() &&
-           dec_ds_wanted(d);
+    /* q11-dec-sand-scaled: a scaled frame too, at its size (the display scales) */
+    show = (!scaled || dec_ds_scaled_on()) && tex && dec_ds_on() &&
+           direct_scanout_sand_usable() && dec_ds_wanted(d);
     if (show && e->show_fd < 0) {
         e->show_fd = fcntl(desc->objects[0].fd, F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC, 0);
     }
@@ -1442,7 +1472,8 @@ static int dec_gpu_write(VirtIOMediaSession *s, VirtIOMediaBuffer *gb,
     if (show) {
         DirectScanout ds = {
             .owner = d, .epoch = d->ds_epoch ? d->ds_epoch : ++dec_ds_epochs,
-            .fd = e->show_fd, .width = w, .height = h,
+            .fd = e->show_fd, .width = fw, .height = fh, /* the frame's size */
+            .src_w = w, .src_h = h, .res = gb->virgl_res,
             .stride = (uint32_t)l->planes[0].pitch,
             .fourcc = l->format, .modifier = mod,
             .offset1 = uv_offset, .pitch1 = (uint32_t)l->planes[1].pitch,
